course: dictionary
lesson: 5065
title: Install: one word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Install means to put something in place and set it up so it is ready to use. It has two main jobs. It can mean putting equipment in place, like a smoke alarm or a new cooker. It can also mean putting a program or app onto a computer, tablet or phone so it works. The words around it tell you which job it is doing.
explain: Read the clues. «Software updates often fix security holes that criminals could use, so installing them protects you.» Software and security holes tell you that installing means adding the update to your device, not fixing a cooker.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. «Pop-ups saying you have won a prize are usually tricks to get information or install harmful software.» Put harmful software onto a computer: that fits, so you have understood it.
explain: Install is a verb, so its form changes: installs, installed, installing. The noun is installation. Remember that only trusted stores are safe places to get apps, and an adult should always be asked first.
fact: Install is a verb: install, installs, installed, installing.
fact: «Install» can mean to put equipment in place and connect it so it is ready to use.
fact: «Install» can also mean to put a program or app onto a computer, tablet or phone so it works.
fact: The noun form is «installation».
fact: Only install apps from trusted stores, and ask an adult first.
exercise: «Software updates often fix security holes, so installing them protects you.» What does installing mean here? | *Adding the update to your device so it works | Throwing the device away | Taking your device apart to look inside | Checking the weather
exercise: «Install smoke alarms and test them.» Which meaning of install is used? | Remove a password | *Put equipment in place so it is ready to use | Put an app onto a phone | Delete a game
exercise: Pop-ups say you have won a prize. What do they try to do? | *Install harmful software on your computer | Update your homework | Install smoke alarms in your home | Give you a free holiday for real
test: Which word is the noun form of install? | *installation | installs | installing | installed
test: Why should you ask an adult before you install an app? | Because adults must buy every app | *Because some apps can install harmful software | Because apps only work on paper | Because apps are always free
exam: Which sentence uses install to mean putting equipment in place? | You must install a password to log in. | The new app will install on your tablet. | *The electrician will install a new cooker in the kitchen. | Please install the update before you play.
